According to Local Rule 5003-1, the clerk may sign his or her name and enter the following without further directive from the court:

(1) an order entering default for failure to plead or otherwise defend under Fed. R. Bankr. P. 7055;
(2) a subpoena for a party not represented by an attorney;
(3) an order of discharge;
(4) an order of dismissal, as directed by Local Rules 2003-1(a), 2082-1(b), 2083-1(e) and 7041-1, or similar dismissal orders arising from the failure of the debtor to respond to a motion to dismiss; and
(5) any other order or document that does not require approval or order by the court under Fed. R. Civ. P. 77(c).

Some examples of areas of special significance may include:
• Ceremonial, burial, or village sites;
• Areas used for hunting, fishing, or trapping;
• Current gathering areas for culturally important or ceremonial materials, such as Basket materials, medicinal plants, or plants used in dances;
• Current gathering areas for subsistence uses, such as mushrooms, berries, acorns, etc.
